  "explanation": "To solve this problem, we need to distribute candies to children based on their ratings. The approach involves two passes through the ratings array. First, we initialize an array 'candies' with 1s, as each child must get at least one candy. Then, we make two passes: one from left to right and another from right to left. In the left-to-right pass, we ensure that if a child has a higher rating than the previous child, they get more candies than the previous child. Similarly, in the right-to-left pass, we ensure that if a child has a higher rating than the next child, they get more candies than the next child. Finally, we sum up the candies array to get the minimum number of candies required.",
